Subject: CommandBuffer::draw: a program's state kept, and a draw made of what changed

A draw was judged and encoded whole every time -- checkTarget, checkStage twice, link, vertexFetch, pushedRanges,
stageTextures, gfxIbos, some 590 words made -- into a stream of its own that appendDeduped then read back to drop
the 9 words in 10 the registers already held. What a draw's program and its kind of pass decide between them is
now worked out at the first draw with that program and kept; the draws after it are judged by what they bind and
written from what differs. The words that reach the command processor are the same, one for one (the golden
streams of every test and scene, both chips' constants, recorded three ways: below).

What is kept, and where:
- ProgramState (render.cpp): for a program in a kind of pass (StateKey: each attachment's format, depth or not,
  every option) the verdicts of checkStage, link and the blend words (ProgramFacts), what each stage needs bound
  (StagePlan), the vertex attributes as vertexFetch reads them, and the words of the groups that are the
  program's alone, as emitDraw wrote them. In the queue (StateCache, by Program::uid) for a program that has a uid,
  so the next command buffer finds it; in the command buffer, beside a copy of the Program compared byte for byte,
  for one made by hand.
- Program::uid: linkProgram gives one, and so does every setter of the C interface that changes a program after
  that (vertex descriptor, blending, samples): a changed program is another program.
- PassCache (OpenPass::cache): the window and sample count checkTarget worked out, the pass's own groups (depth
  and stencil buffer, colour targets, MSAA, RB_RENDER_CNTL, LRZ) by what a program draws into, a fetch's
  descriptors of the attachments, and for each of the pass's streams a Cursor: the words it last held of each
  kept group and the numbers the last draw's own groups were made of.
- DrawCache (CommandBuffer): the states at hand by uid, the facts' scratch.

A draw with a kept state:
- fastFacts and fastTables are drawFacts' rules for what a draw brings -- bindings, counts, viewport, scissor,
  depth and stencil state, the index buffer -- and write the texture, sampler and IBO descriptors straight into the
  draw's table (a texture's sampled descriptor is made once: Texture::sampledWords). Whatever they are not sure of
  goes the long way, where drawFacts judges it and refuses it by its sentence.
- emitFast walks the groups in the order a draw has them. A kept group whose words are the ones the stream last
  held for it is passed over; one that differs goes through the register shadow (DedupSink: appendDeduped's rule
  applied as the words are made, no stream in between). A group made of the draw's numbers is made when the
  numbers are not the last draw's. The stages' loads and HLSQ_INVALIDATE_CMD, which no shadow drops, are appended
  as they are, every draw. That a group passed over is one the shadow would have dropped whole stands on the
  groups writing registers of their own, which a test holds them to.
- keep() and use() take a reference and remember what they were just given: a draw names the buffers and textures
  of the draw before it. The submission names the same buffers (the golden streams' names).

The first draw with a program, a draw with private memory, an indirect draw, one that counts samples and any pass
without deduplication go the long way as before (drawFacts, emitDraw through DedupSink).

Held to the long way three times over:
- CommandBuffer::verifyDraws: every draw taken from a kept state is also written whole, through a copy of the
  shadow as it was, and the words and the table's bytes compared. The tests run with it on; `tests --unchecked` runs
  them again as a device does.
- CommandBuffer::keepStates(false) (hakios_metal_draw_states, `tests --long`, `drawbench --long`): no kept state at
  all. `make -f tools/dev.mk check` compares the golden sums of all three.
- tests/draw_state_test.cpp: the cases a kept state is wrong in if kept wrongly, and random frames -- half of each
  draw's kind made anew, half the draw before with one thing changed, a quarter then wrong in one thing --
  recorded both ways: the same draws taken, the same refusals by the same sentences, the same passes, the same
  submissions (39 692 draws taken, 26 778 of them from kept states, 6 388 refused, a chip). Sixteen bugs seeded
  one at a time into the kept path (a check dropped from fastFacts, a field left out of a Cursor's comparison, a
  buffer not named, a stale slot) each fail it.

append(): what the appended buffer remembers having named and kept is forgotten with its lists.

Host, A610 constants, us a draw / heap allocations a draw (drawbench, the scenes of the C interface with the
phone's own stages): S 18.97 / 64.7 -> 6.4 / 6.2, T 10.88 / 38.3 -> 3.9 / 5.8 (quick runs; the table is in the
report).


